{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3169","artifact_type":"codebase-analysis","name":"plan/codebase-testing-duplicate-detection-content-match.md@sha256:552e09edc9c4e0eb1fa140d222bdb2b83e403c3046c9063ba23c9cc2b45ee589"},"owner_reference":"3169","content":"# Codebase Analysis: Testing for Duplicate Detection (Issue #3169)\n\n## Test Structure Overview\n\n### Test Classes and Coverage\n\n#### 1. `tests/test_backlog_core_parsing.py::TestFindFuzzyDuplicates` (~14 tests, lines 1020-1109)\n\n**Purpose:** Unit tests for `find_fuzzy_duplicates(title, items, threshold)` function\n\n**Tests and assertions:**\n\n| Test | Assertion | Algorithm Dependency |\n|------|-----------|---------------------|\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_exact_match_returns_one_result` | Exact title match returns single tuple | SequenceMatcher ratio=1.0 |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_exact_match_ratio_is_one` | Ratio >= 1.0 for exact match | SequenceMatcher edge case |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_similar_title_detected_above_threshold` | \"fuzzy duplicate detection\" matches \"fuzzy duplicate detection\" at ratio >= 0.80 | SequenceMatcher >= threshold behavior |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_dissimilar_title_returns_empty` | \"SAM Error Recovery\" vs \"Validate Terminal Browser\" = no match | SequenceMatcher < threshold |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_skips_items_with_skip_true` | Items with `skip=True` are excluded from results | `item.skip` guard clause |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_strips_commit_prefix_before_comparison` | \"feat: SAM Error Recovery\" matches \"SAM Error Recovery\" | `normalize_issue_title()` prefix stripping |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_new_title_commit_prefix_stripped` | \"fix: SAM Error Recovery\" matches \"SAM Error Recovery\" | `normalize_issue_title()` on new title |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_returns_tuples_of_title_ratio_path` | Returns `(existing_title, ratio: float, file_path: str)` | Return type structure |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_sorted_by_ratio_descending` | Multiple matches sorted by ratio descending | `matches.sort(key=..., reverse=True)` |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_empty_title_returns_empty` | Empty new title returns `[]` | `if not normalized_new: return []` |\n| `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_custom_threshold_respected` | With threshold=0.0, all items match | Threshold comparison logic |\n\n**Additional edge case class:** `TestFindFuzzyDuplicatesEdgeCases` (line 1700)\n- `test_find_fuzzy_duplicates_skips_items_with_empty_title` \u2014 Items with empty title are skipped\n- (Others exist; pattern shows empty/boundary checks are covered)\n\n**Test data design:**\n- Uses hardcoded BacklogItem objects with fixed titles and file paths\n- Titles chosen to test:\n  - Exact matches: \"SAM Error Recovery\"\n  - Near-matches: Similar word sequences above/below 0.80 threshold\n  - Dissimilar: Completely different semantic domain (browser vs SAM)\n  - Edge cases: Empty strings, commit-prefixed titles\n- No test data from issue #3169's failing examples (\"CI check for drift...\" pair)\n\n**What tests LOCK in:**\n1. Algorithm: `difflib.SequenceMatcher` is used; any change requires test updates\n2. Threshold: 0.80 is the expected default; tests hardcode this value\n3. Prefix handling: `normalize_issue_title()` must strip conventional-commit prefixes\n4. Return type: `list[tuple[str, float, str]]` carrying (title, ratio, path)\n5. Skip logic: Items with `item.skip == True` must be excluded\n6. No description/body matching: Tests only pass title; no tests verify searching descriptions\n\n---\n\n#### 2. `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py::TestAddItemDuplicateDetection` (~3 tests, lines 645-693)\n\n**Purpose:** Integration tests for `add_item` with duplicate detection\n\n**Tests:**\n\n| Test | Assertion | Code Path |\n|------|-----------|-----------|\n| `test_add_item_raises_on_fuzzy_duplicate` | `add_item()` raises `DuplicateItemError` when similar item exists | `_check_for_duplicates()` inside `add_item()` |\n| `test_add_item_force_bypasses_duplicate_check` | `add_item(..., force=True)` succeeds despite duplicate | `if force: return` in `_check_for_duplicates()` |\n| `test_add_item_no_duplicate_succeeds` | `add_item()` succeeds when no similar items exist | Happy path; empty backlog |\n\n**Test setup:**\n- Uses `_write_item()` helper to seed backlog with existing items\n- Mocks `try_get_github` to return None (skip GitHub issue creation)\n- Uses temporary file-system backend (InMemoryBackend via fixture)\n\n**Test data:**\n- Existing: \"Implement Error Recovery\"\n- New (similar): \"Implement Error Recovery Logic\" \u2014 designed to exceed 0.80 threshold\n- New (unique): \"Completely Unique Novel Feature\" \u2014 designed to fail to match\n\n**What tests LOCK in:**\n1. Timing: Duplicate check runs inside `add_item()` at write time\n2. Exception type: `DuplicateItemError` is raised (not returned, not logged)\n3. Force bypass: `force=True` parameter disables the check entirely\n4. Result structure: Success case returns dict with 'file_path' key (unrelated to duplicate detection but part of same function)\n\n**What tests do NOT cover:**\n- Cache staleness (concurrent writes, items created by other sessions)\n- Result shape of the exception (what caller receives when catching)\n- Inability to act on the result (no path to extend existing item)\n- Search-based detection alternative\n- Timing gap (effort already spent before check fires)\n\n---\n\n#### 3. `tests/test_backlog_core_models.py::TestDuplicateItemError` (~7 tests, lines 526-568)\n\n**Purpose:** Tests for `DuplicateItemError` exception class\n\n**Tests:**\n\n| Test | Assertion |\n|------|-----------|\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_stores_duplicates` | `.duplicates` attribute preserves input list of tuples |\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_message_contains_title` | Exception message includes matched item titles |\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_message_contains_percentage` | Exception message includes similarity percentage (e.g. \"95%\") |\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_message_format_single` | Single duplicate formats as `'Similar backlog items found: \"Alpha\" (80%)'` |\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_message_format_multiple` | Multiple duplicates include all titles and percentages in message |\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_is_raised_as_backlog_error` | Can be caught as `BacklogError` base class |\n| `test_duplicate_item_error_percentage_rounding` | Parametrized test: ratios 1.0, 0.90, 0.85, 0.80 format as 100%, 90%, 85%, 80% |\n\n**Test data:**\n- Single tuple: `(\"My Feature\", 0.95, \"/path.md\")`\n- Multiple: `[(\"Alpha\", 0.80, \"/a.md\"), (\"Beta\", 1.0, \"/b.md\")]`\n- Percentages tested: 1.0, 0.90, 0.85, 0.80 (edge cases around threshold)\n\n**What tests LOCK in:**\n1. Exception carries `duplicates: list[tuple[str, float, str]]`\n2. Message format: `f'\"{t}\" ({int(r * 100)}%)'` for each tuple\n3. Inheritance: Is-a `BacklogError`\n4. Rounding: `int(ratio * 100)` converts to percentage (banker's rounding behavior)\n\n**What tests do NOT cover:**\n- `.duplicates` content is usable by caller (they do test that it's stored, but not that caller can do anything with it)\n- File path actually identifies a work item the caller can fetch/extend\n- Scenario where multiple matches exist but only one is actionable\n\n---\n\n## Test File Organization\n\n### `test_backlog_core_parsing.py`\n- **Lines 1-50:** Imports and test data\n- **Lines 1020-1140:** `TestFindFuzzyDuplicates` and `TestNormalizeIssueTitle` classes\n- **~14 duplicate-related tests** plus many for unrelated parsing functions\n- **Isolation:** Pure function tests; no file I/O, no GitHub, no backend dependency\n\n### `test_backlog_core_operations.py`\n- **Lines 77-133:** Helper functions for test setup (`_seed_items`, `_write_item`, etc.)\n- **Lines 645-693:** `TestAddItemDuplicateDetection` class\n- **~3 duplicate-related tests** plus ~60+ tests for other `add_item` paths\n- **Isolation:** Uses `InMemoryBackend` via fixture; mocks GitHub calls\n- **State:** Autouse fixture redirects `BACKLOG_DIR` to `tmp_path` per test\n\n### `test_backlog_core_models.py`\n- **Lines 526-568:** `TestDuplicateItemError` class\n- **~7 duplicate-related tests** plus many for other model classes\n- **Isolation:** Pure unit tests; no I/O, no backend, no GitHub\n- **Coverage:** Error class formatting and inheritance\n\n---\n\n## Current Test Assumptions\n\n### Algorithm Assumptions\n1. **SequenceMatcher is the right algorithm:** All tests assume `difflib.SequenceMatcher` on normalized titles\n2. **Threshold = 0.80:** Tests hardcoded to expect this threshold; changing it requires updating test data\n3. **Title-only matching:** No tests verify description or content matching\n4. **Normalization function is correct:** Tests assume `normalize_issue_title()` correctly strips prefixes\n5. **Result format is immutable:** Tests hardcode expected `(title, ratio, path)` tuple structure\n\n### Behavioral Assumptions\n1. **Timing is correct:** Tests assume write-time checking is correct; no tests verify pre-write timing\n2. **Exception path is correct:** Tests verify that `DuplicateItemError` is raised; no tests verify alternative handling\n3. **Force bypass is sufficient:** Tests verify `force=True` disables check; no tests verify whether this is the right escape hatch\n4. **Skip items are skipped:** Tests verify `item.skip == True` excludes items; no tests verify this is the right status filter\n\n### Data Assumptions\n1. **In-memory backend is representative:** Tests use `InMemoryBackend`; no tests verify behavior with GitHub cache staleness\n2. **Test titles are representative:** Test data uses near-duplicates at 0.80 boundary; no tests use semantically identical items with different wording (issue #3169's failure case)\n\n---\n\n## Test Gaps (Not Verified by Current Tests)\n\n### Algorithm Gaps\n- No test data matching issue #3169's documented failure pair:\n  - \"CI check for drift between MCP server tool lists and agent frontmatter `tools:` entries\" (0.4683 ratio, no match)\n  - \"Agent `tools:` frontmatter drifts from MCP server tool lists with no enforcement and silent failure\"\n  - Tests would fail if `SequenceMatcher` is replaced with semantic search\n\n### Cache Staleness Gap\n- No test verifies behavior when `list_work_items()` returns stale cache\n- No test mocks concurrent session creating a duplicate that's not yet in cache\n- No test verifies error message distinguishes \"no duplicate\" from \"could not check\"\n\n### Result Usability Gap\n- Tests verify exception is raised and `.duplicates` is stored, but NOT that caller can:\n  - Fetch the full item to read description/content\n  - Get item reference needed for `groom-backlog-item`\n  - Parse the exception to identify which existing item to extend\n\n### Timing Gap\n- No test verifies that check runs at the right point in workflow\n- No test captures the issue that effort is already spent by the time check fires\n\n### Search Alternative Gap\n- No test verifies that `backlog_list(search=...)` could be used for detection\n- No test compares `SequenceMatcher` result vs search-based result for same item pair\n\n### CLI Coverage Gap\n- No test verifies that `backlog list --search` is unavailable (gap exists but is not tested)\n\n---\n\n## Deliberate Test Design Choices\n\n### Why Tests Use Low-Data Volume\n- `TestFindFuzzyDuplicates` uses single items or pairs, not production backlog\n- Rationale: Pure function; no scaling concerns; focus on edge cases around 0.80 threshold\n- Trade-off: Tests don't verify behavior over large item sets (no N+1 search patterns)\n\n### Why Tests Use Near-Duplicates\n- Test titles designed to exceed/miss 0.80 threshold (e.g., \"...Error Recovery\" vs \"...Error Recovery Logic\")\n- Rationale: Test the threshold behavior specifically\n- Trade-off: Don't test semantically identical items with different wording (issue #3169's failure case)\n\n### Why Integration Tests Use Mocked GitHub\n- `test_add_item_*` mocks `try_get_github`\n- Rationale: Isolate duplicate detection from GitHub mutation/sync complexity\n- Trade-off: Don't test behavior with real GitHub cache or live issues\n\n---\n\n## Breaking Changes Required by Issue #3169 Fix\n\nAny implementation of #3169 will require updates to:\n\n1. **`TestFindFuzzyDuplicates` tests:** If algorithm changes from `SequenceMatcher` to semantic search\n   - Current tests verify character-sequence matches\n   - Semantic search would pass different test data (issue #3169 example pair)\n   - Threshold value may change or become domain-specific\n\n2. **`TestAddItemDuplicateDetection` tests:** If timing changes from write-time to pre-write\n   - Current tests call `add_item` expecting immediate exception\n   - Pre-write check would require separate invocation/return path\n   - Tests would need to verify that check happens *before* `add_item`\n\n3. **`TestDuplicateItemError` tests:** If result shape changes from `(title, ratio, path)` to `(item_ref, item_content, match_context)`\n   - Current tests verify message formatting from (title, ratio)\n   - New shape would require different formatting tests\n   - Caller behavior changes from \"display titles\" to \"display item references\"\n\n4. **New tests required:** For search-based detection and cache refresh behavior\n   - Verify `from_github=True` refresh works\n   - Verify search query results match expected items\n   - Verify match_context includes field and snippet information\n\n---\n\n## Test Dependencies on Current Implementation\n\n### Hard Dependencies (Will Fail on Change)\n- `difflib.SequenceMatcher` algorithm\n- Threshold value 0.80\n- Return type `list[tuple[str, float, str]]`\n- Exception class name `DuplicateItemError`\n- Exception raised (not logged/returned)\n- `item.skip == True` exclusion\n\n### Soft Dependencies (May Need Updates)\n- Message format `\"Similar backlog items found: ...\"`\n- Percentage rounding behavior `int(r * 100)`\n- Inheritance from `BacklogError`\n- Timing: write-time execution\n\n### No Dependencies (Can Change Freely)\n- Internal normalization function behavior (tests don't directly verify it)\n- Specific backends used (tests use InMemoryBackend but concept applies to all)\n- File path structure in returned tuples (tests don't verify path format, only that it's a string)"}